---
template_id: openagreements-privacy-policy
name: Consumer Privacy Policy
category: data-compliance
description: >-
  Configurable national consumer privacy-policy template that assembles the union of U.S.
  state privacy-disclosure duties, gated by a business's coverage and data-practice facts.
source_url: >-
  https://github.com/open-agreements/open-agreements/tree/main/templates/openagreements-privacy-policy
version: "0.1"
license: CC-BY-4.0
allow_derivatives: true
attribution_text: >-
  Adapted from the OpenAgreements privacy-policy specification. Licensed under CC BY 4.0.
layout_id: cover-standard-signature-v1
style_id: openagreements-default-v1
document:
  title: Privacy Policy
  label: OpenAgreements Consumer Privacy Policy
  version: "0.1"
  license: Free to use under CC BY 4.0
  presentation: traditional
  include_cloud_doc_line: true
  defined_term_highlight_mode: definition_site_only
sections:
  cover_terms:
    section_label: Policy Summary
    heading_title: Policy Summary
  standard_terms:
    section_label: Privacy Policy
    heading_title: Privacy Policy
  signature:
    section_label: Contact
    heading_title: How to Contact Us
omitted_clauses: drop
fields:
  - name: business_legal_name
    type: string
    description: Legal name of the business (the controller) that this privacy policy describes.
    display_label: Business Legal Name
    section: Business
  - name: business_contact_email
    type: string
    description: An email address consumers can use to reach the business about this policy or their privacy rights.
    display_label: Contact Email
    section: Business
  - name: business_postal_address
    type: string
    description: A postal address consumers can use to reach the business about this policy or their privacy rights.
    display_label: Postal Address
    section: Business
  - name: privacy_request_url
    type: string
    description: The web address or channel where consumers submit privacy-rights requests.
    display_label: Privacy Request Link
    section: Requests
  - name: appeal_request_url
    type: string
    description: The web address or channel where consumers appeal a refused privacy-rights request.
    display_label: Appeal Link
    section: Requests
  - name: rights_response_days
    type: number
    description: >-
      The number of days within which the business responds to a privacy-rights request. The
      common VCDPA-family clock is 45 days (the union-strictest common deadline); set it shorter
      if a stricter in-scope state's deadline binds the business.
    display_label: Rights Response Days
    default: 45
    default_value_rationale: >-
      45 days is the common comprehensive-privacy-act response clock; it is the safe national
      default until a narrower in-scope state deadline applies.
    section: Requests
  - name: appeal_response_days
    type: number
    description: >-
      The number of days within which the business responds to an appeal of a refused request.
      The Florida (FDBR) appeal window is 60 days (the union-strictest common deadline); set it
      shorter if a stricter in-scope state's deadline binds the business.
    display_label: Appeal Response Days
    default: 60
    default_value_rationale: >-
      60 days is the FDBR appeal window and the safe national default until a narrower in-scope
      state deadline applies.
    section: Requests
  - name: policy_effective_date
    type: string
    description: The date this privacy policy takes effect.
    display_label: Effective Date
    section: Dates
  - name: policy_last_updated
    type: string
    description: The date this privacy policy was last updated.
    display_label: Last Updated
    section: Dates
  - name: personal_data_categories
    type: string
    description: >-
      The categories of personal data the business processes, as a comma-separated phrase
      (e.g. "identifiers, contact details, device and usage data, purchase history").
    display_label: Personal Data Categories
    section: Disclosures
  - name: sensitive_data_categories
    type: string
    description: >-
      The sensitive-data categories the business processes, called out separately, as a
      comma-separated phrase (e.g. "precise geolocation, health data"). Required when the
      business processes sensitive data; the sensitive-data DISCLOSURE sentence is gated on this
      field being non-empty, and the sensitive-data CONSENT clause is gated separately on the
      derived field show_sensitive_consent.
    display_label: Sensitive Data Categories
    section: Disclosures
  - name: processing_purposes
    type: string
    description: >-
      The purposes for which the business processes personal data, as a comma-separated phrase
      (e.g. "providing and improving our services, processing transactions, security and fraud
      prevention, communicating with you").
    display_label: Processing Purposes
    section: Disclosures
  - name: third_party_categories
    type: string
    description: >-
      The categories of third parties with whom the business shares personal data, described in
      enough detail for a consumer to understand what type of entity each is, as a comma-separated
      phrase (e.g. "payment processors, cloud-hosting providers, analytics vendors").
    display_label: Third-Party Recipient Categories
    section: Disclosures
  - name: data_sources
    type: string
    description: >-
      The sources from which the business collects personal data, as a comma-separated phrase
      (e.g. "directly from you, automatically from your device, from our service providers").
    display_label: Data Sources
    section: Disclosures
  - name: covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when a comprehensive consumer-privacy act covers the business. Feeds the derived gates
      show_rights_machinery, show_profiling_optout, show_uoom, show_sale_optout, and
      show_sensitive_consent. Default true (safe maximal); a business covered by no privacy regime
      switches it off.
    display_label: Covered by a comprehensive state privacy law
    help: >-
      Check this if a comprehensive state consumer-privacy law — such as California's, Virginia's,
      or Colorado's — applies to your business.
    default: true
    default_value_rationale: >-
      Defaults true so the consumer-rights machinery is included by default under the national
      assumption; a business covered by no comprehensive act switches it off to avoid gold-plating.
    section: Coverage
    ai_only: true
  - name: covered_by_limited_scope_notice_regime
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when a limited-scope notice/sale regime covers the business without a comprehensive act
      (e.g. a Nevada website operator, a Rhode Island commercial site that sells data, Florida's
      narrow act). Feeds the derived gates show_sale_optout and show_sensitive_consent. Default
      true (safe maximal).
    display_label: Covered by a narrower privacy or data-sale law
    help: >-
      Check this if a narrower state privacy or data-sale law applies to your business but a
      comprehensive one does not — for example, a Nevada website operator or a business that sells
      data under Florida's or Rhode Island's laws.
    default: true
    default_value_rationale: >-
      Defaults true so limited-scope sale and sensitive-data duties are included by default; a
      business covered by no regime at all switches it off.
    section: Coverage
    ai_only: true
  - name: honors_universal_opt_out_signal
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      Whether the site actually honors a universal opt-out signal (e.g. Global Privacy
      Control). An operational fact; feeds the derived gate show_uoom (= covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act
      AND honors_universal_opt_out_signal). A false value suppresses the clause rather than
      asserting honoring the business has not implemented.
    display_label: Honors universal opt-out signals
    help: >-
      Check this if your website honors — actually acts on — universal opt-out signals such as
      Global Privacy Control, not merely detects them.
    default: true
    default_value_rationale: >-
      Defaults true because honoring a universal opt-out signal is effectively mandatory for a
      comprehensively-covered national business; set false only as a remediation item, which
      suppresses the clause to avoid a false assertion.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: processes_sensitive_data
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business processes sensitive data. Feeds the derived gate show_sensitive_consent
      (= (covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act OR covered_by_limited_scope_notice_regime) AND
      processes_sensitive_data).
    display_label: Processes sensitive personal data
    help: >-
      Check this if your business processes sensitive personal data — such as precise geolocation,
      health information, or data revealing race, religion, or sexual orientation.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business affirmatively processes sensitive data.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: sells_personal_data
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business sells personal data. Feeds the derived gate show_sale_optout
      (= (covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act OR covered_by_limited_scope_notice_regime) AND
      (sells_personal_data OR processes_for_targeted_advertising)).
    display_label: Sells personal data
    help: >-
      Check this if your business sells personal data — that is, shares it with third parties in
      exchange for money or other valuable consideration.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business affirmatively sells personal data.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: sells_sensitive_personal_data
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business sells SENSITIVE personal data specifically. Gates (via include-when)
      the Texas scripted sale-notice clause, which renders the fixed statutory notice
      (Tex. Bus. & Com. Code § 541.106). A practice-gated module, independent of the coverage flags.
    display_label: Sells sensitive personal data
    help: >-
      Check this if your business specifically sells sensitive personal data to third parties.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business affirmatively sells sensitive personal data.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: processes_for_targeted_advertising
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business processes personal data for targeted advertising. Feeds the derived
      gate show_sale_optout (= (covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act OR
      covered_by_limited_scope_notice_regime) AND (sells_personal_data OR
      processes_for_targeted_advertising)).
    display_label: Uses data for targeted advertising
    help: >-
      Check this if your business uses personal data to show advertising selected based on activity
      across other websites or apps.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business affirmatively processes data for targeted advertising.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: processes_for_profiling
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business profiles consumers in furtherance of decisions that produce legal or
      similarly significant effects. Feeds the derived gate show_profiling_optout
      (= covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act AND processes_for_profiling).
    display_label: Profiles consumers for significant decisions
    help: >-
      Check this if your business profiles consumers to help make decisions that produce legal or
      similarly significant effects about them.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business affirmatively performs significant-effect profiling.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: has_minor_users
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business directs services to, or has actual knowledge of, minor users. Sole
      input to the derived gate minors_active (see #1304).
    display_label: Directs services to, or knows of, minor users
    help: >-
      Check this if your business directs its services to minors or has actual knowledge that
      minors use them.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business affirmatively directs services to, or knows of, minor users.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: as_of_date
    type: date
    description: >-
      The date this policy is generated or takes effect, reserved for temporal gating of
      future-effective components. No active gate currently consumes it: the minors_active date
      condition (SC Act 96, live 2026-02-05) is permanently satisfied and was dropped from the
      formula (see #1304). When unset, resolves to the generation date at fill time.
    section: Coverage
    ai_only: true
  - name: collects_biometric_identifiers
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business collects biometric identifiers. Gates (via include-when) the biometric
      retention-policy and biometric written-release clauses. Independent of the coverage flags.
    display_label: Collects biometric identifiers
    help: >-
      Check this if your business collects biometric identifiers, such as fingerprints or face- or
      voice-recognition data.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business affirmatively collects biometric identifiers.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: collects_consumer_health_data
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business collects consumer health data. Gates (via include-when) the
      consumer-health-data policy and health-data consent clauses. Independent of the coverage flags.
    display_label: Collects consumer health data
    help: >-
      Check this if your business collects consumer health data that falls outside HIPAA-regulated
      protected health information.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business affirmatively collects consumer health data.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: is_website_operator
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business is a covered website operator (e.g. under the Nevada operator regime).
      Gates (via include-when) the website-operator notice clause.
    display_label: Operates a covered website or online service
    help: >-
      Check this if your business operates a website or online service covered by a state operator
      notice law, such as Nevada's.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business is a covered website operator.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: has_known_child_users
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business has known child users (under 13). Gates (via include-when) the COPPA
      routing clause. Federal; independent of the coverage flags.
    display_label: Has known child users under 13
    help: >-
      Check this if your business has actual knowledge that children under 13 use its services.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business has actual knowledge of child users under 13.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: is_data_broker
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      True when the business knowingly sells or licenses to third parties the personal data of
      consumers with whom it has no direct relationship. Gates (via include-when) the data-broker
      opt-out clause.
    display_label: Is a data broker
    help: >-
      Check this if your business knowingly sells or licenses to third parties the personal data of
      consumers it has no direct relationship with.
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Conservative false default; set true only when the business is a data broker.
    section: Practices
    ai_only: true
  - name: show_rights_machinery
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      Derived gate. Compute as: covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act. Gates the consumer-rights
      catalog, rights-request method, response-timeline, and appeal clauses.
    derived_gate: "covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act"
    default: true
    default_value_rationale: Mirrors covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act, which defaults true under the national assumption.
    section: Derived Gates
    ai_only: true
  - name: show_profiling_optout
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      Derived gate. Compute as: covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act AND processes_for_profiling.
      Gates the profiling opt-out clause.
    derived_gate: "covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act AND processes_for_profiling"
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Mirrors the conjunction; processes_for_profiling defaults false, so this defaults false.
    section: Derived Gates
    ai_only: true
  - name: show_uoom
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      Derived gate. Compute as: covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act AND
      honors_universal_opt_out_signal. Gates the universal-opt-out-signal clause.
    derived_gate: "covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act AND honors_universal_opt_out_signal"
    default: true
    default_value_rationale: Mirrors the conjunction; both inputs default true, so this defaults true.
    section: Derived Gates
    ai_only: true
  - name: show_sale_optout
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      Derived gate. Compute as: (covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act OR
      covered_by_limited_scope_notice_regime) AND (sells_personal_data OR
      processes_for_targeted_advertising). Gates the sale/targeted-advertising opt-out clause.
    derived_gate: "(covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act OR covered_by_limited_scope_notice_regime) AND (sells_personal_data OR processes_for_targeted_advertising)"
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Mirrors the expression; sells_personal_data and processes_for_targeted_advertising both default false, so this defaults false.
    section: Derived Gates
    ai_only: true
  - name: show_sensitive_consent
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      Derived gate. Compute as: (covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act OR
      covered_by_limited_scope_notice_regime) AND processes_sensitive_data. Gates the
      sensitive-data consent clause.
    derived_gate: "(covered_by_comprehensive_privacy_act OR covered_by_limited_scope_notice_regime) AND processes_sensitive_data"
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Mirrors the expression; processes_sensitive_data defaults false, so this defaults false.
    section: Derived Gates
    ai_only: true
  - name: minors_active
    type: boolean
    description: >-
      Derived gate. Compute as: has_minor_users. Gates the minor-user disclosures clause. (This gate
      once also required as_of_date >= 2026-02-05 — the earliest live minors component, SC Act 96 —
      but that date passed, permanently satisfying the temporal term, so it was dropped from the
      formula during #1304.)
    derived_gate: "has_minor_users"
    default: false
    default_value_rationale: Mirrors has_minor_users, which defaults false, so this defaults false.
    section: Derived Gates
    ai_only: true
priority_fields:
  - business_legal_name
  - policy_effective_date
  - personal_data_categories
artifact_kind: policy
capabilities:
  - create
  - review
  - render
party_roles: []
signature_roles: []
mutation_policy: fields_only
maturity: experimental
---

# Privacy Policy

{% agreement-section type="cover_terms" %}
## Policy Summary

The summary below states the key facts about this Privacy Policy and how to reach us.

{% cover-terms %}
{% cover-term kind="row" label="Business" field="business_legal_name" /%}
{% cover-term kind="row" label="Contact Email" field="business_contact_email" include-when="business_contact_email" /%}
{% cover-term kind="row" label="Postal Address" field="business_postal_address" include-when="business_postal_address" /%}
{% cover-term kind="row" label="Effective Date" field="policy_effective_date" /%}
{% cover-term kind="row" label="Last Updated" field="policy_last_updated" include-when="policy_last_updated" /%}
{% cover-term kind="row" label="Privacy Request Link" field="privacy_request_url" include-when="privacy_request_url" /%}
{% /cover-terms %}
{% /agreement-section %}

{% agreement-section type="standard_terms" %}
## Privacy Policy

{% clause id="who-we-are" %}
### Who We Are

This Privacy Policy explains how {% field name="business_legal_name" /%} collects, uses, and shares your Personal Data. If you have questions about this policy or your privacy rights, contact us at {% field name="business_contact_email" /%} or {% field name="business_postal_address" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="effective-date" %}
### Effective Date

This Privacy Policy is effective as of {% field name="policy_effective_date" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="information-we-collect" %}
### Information We Collect

We collect the following categories of Personal Data: {% field name="personal_data_categories" /%}. We collect this information from the following sources: {% field name="data_sources" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="sensitive-data-disclosure" include-when="sensitive_data_categories" %}
### Sensitive Information

Some of what we collect is Sensitive Data. We identify those categories here separately: {% field name="sensitive_data_categories" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="why-we-collect-it" %}
### Why We Collect It

We process Personal Data for the following purposes: {% field name="processing_purposes" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="how-we-share-it" %}
### How We Share It

We may share Personal Data with the following categories of third parties: {% field name="third_party_categories" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="your-privacy-rights" include-when="show_rights_machinery" %}
### Your Privacy Rights

If you are a Consumer in a state with a comprehensive privacy law, you have the right to: confirm whether we process your Personal Data and access it; correct inaccuracies; delete it; obtain a portable copy; and opt out of Targeted Advertising, the Sale of your Personal Data, and Profiling in furtherance of decisions that produce legal or similarly significant effects. You may also opt out of our collection of Sensitive Data and of the use of voice- or facial-recognition features.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="how-to-exercise-your-rights" include-when="show_rights_machinery" %}
### How to Exercise Your Rights

To exercise any of these rights, submit a request at {% field name="privacy_request_url" /%}. We will not deny you goods or services, or otherwise discriminate against you, for exercising them.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="our-response" include-when="show_rights_machinery" %}
### Our Response

We will respond to your request without undue delay and within {% field name="rights_response_days" /%} days of receipt. When reasonably necessary, we may extend this period once by 15 additional days, and we will tell you of the extension and the reason within the initial period.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="appeals" include-when="show_rights_machinery" %}
### Appeals

If we decline to act on your request, you may appeal at {% field name="appeal_request_url" /%}. We will respond in writing, with the reasons for our decision, within {% field name="appeal_response_days" /%} days.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="sale-and-targeted-advertising" include-when="show_sale_optout" %}
### Sale of Data and Targeted Advertising

Where we sell your Personal Data or process it for Targeted Advertising, you may opt out of those activities at any time at {% field name="privacy_request_url" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="texas-sensitive-data-sale-notice" include-when="sells_sensitive_personal_data" %}
### Notice of Sale of Sensitive Data

NOTICE: We may sell your sensitive personal data.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="profiling" include-when="show_profiling_optout" %}
### Profiling

We use Profiling in furtherance of decisions that produce legal or similarly significant effects concerning you. You may opt out of this profiling at {% field name="privacy_request_url" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="universal-opt-out-signals" include-when="show_uoom" %}
### Universal Opt-Out Signals

[[Universal Opt-Out Signal]] means a user-selected browser or device control that communicates an opt-out preference, such as the Global Privacy Control.

We recognize and honor a Universal Opt-Out Signal, such as the Global Privacy Control (GPC), as a valid request to opt out of Targeted Advertising and the Sale of Personal Data from the browser or device that sends it.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="sensitive-data-consent" include-when="show_sensitive_consent" %}
### Sensitive Data

We obtain your opt-in consent before collecting or processing the following categories of Sensitive Data: {% field name="sensitive_data_categories" /%}. You may withdraw that consent at any time at {% field name="privacy_request_url" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="children-under-13" include-when="has_known_child_users" %}
### Children Under 13

We do not knowingly collect Personal Data from a child under 13 without verifiable parental consent, and we handle any such data in accordance with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA).

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="biometric-data-retention" include-when="collects_biometric_identifiers" %}
### Biometric Data Retention

[[Biometric Identifier]] means a retina or iris scan, fingerprint, voiceprint, or scan of hand or face geometry.

We maintain this written, publicly available policy establishing our retention schedule and guidelines for permanently destroying Biometric Identifiers. We destroy a Biometric Identifier when the initial purpose for collecting it has been satisfied or within three years of your last interaction with us, whichever occurs first.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="biometric-consent" include-when="collects_biometric_identifiers" %}
### Biometric Consent

Before we collect a Biometric Identifier, we inform you in writing that we are collecting it, the specific purpose, and the length of time we will store and use it, and we obtain your written release.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="consumer-health-data" include-when="collects_consumer_health_data" %}
### Consumer Health Data

[[Consumer Health Data]] means Personal Data that identifies a Consumer's past, present, or future physical or mental health status.

We collect the categories of Consumer Health Data listed in Information We Collect, use that data for the purposes listed in Why We Collect It, and share it with the third parties and affiliates listed in How We Share It. You may exercise your rights over this data at {% field name="privacy_request_url" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="consent-for-health-data" include-when="collects_consumer_health_data" %}
### Consent for Health Data

We do not collect Consumer Health Data except with your consent for a specified purpose, or to the extent necessary to provide a product or service you have requested from us.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="website-notice" include-when="is_website_operator" %}
### Website Notice

Through our website we collect the categories of covered information described above and may share them with the third-party categories described above. You may review and request changes to your information, where that process is available, at {% field name="privacy_request_url" /%}. We notify you of material changes as described in Changes to This Policy. Third parties may collect covered information about your online activities over time and across different websites when you use our website.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="minors" include-when="minors_active" %}
### Minors

Where we direct services to, or have actual knowledge of, users who are minors, we provide the additional disclosures required by applicable state law, including our minors' design and safety practices, the privacy protections we apply to minors, and the parental tools we make available.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="data-broker-opt-out" include-when="is_data_broker" %}
### Data Broker Opt-Out

[[Data Broker]] means a business that knowingly sells or licenses to third parties the Personal Data of Consumers with whom it has no direct relationship.

As a Data Broker, we let you opt out of our collection, sale, or licensing of your Personal Data. You or your authorized agent may submit an opt-out request at {% field name="privacy_request_url" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="keeping-this-policy-current" %}
### Keeping This Policy Current

We review this Privacy Policy and refresh its disclosures at least once every 12 months. It was last updated on {% field name="policy_last_updated" /%}.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="changes-to-this-policy" %}
### Changes to This Policy

When we make a material change to this Privacy Policy, we will revise it, update the Effective Date above, and take reasonable steps to notify you of the change.

{% /clause %}

{% clause id="definitions" type="definitions" %}
### Definitions

[[Personal Data]] means information that is linked or reasonably linkable to an identified or identifiable individual.

[[Sensitive Data]] means Personal Data that receives heightened protection under applicable law. The Sensitive Information section identifies the categories we collect.

[[Consumer]] means an individual who is a resident of a state and acts in an individual or household context.

[[Sale]] means the exchange of Personal Data for monetary or other valuable consideration.

[[Targeted Advertising]] means advertising selected based on Personal Data obtained from a Consumer's activity across nonaffiliated sites or applications.

[[Profiling]] means automated processing used to evaluate, analyze, or predict an individual's characteristics.

{% /clause %}
{% /agreement-section %}

